Give the quadrant diagram of concept-numbers.tex something the model holds.
The diagram of the quadrant numbers (Figure "Quadrant Numbering for Branch
Cuts") is an \halign inside a cell of another \halign, set in $$ ... $$ for
the line drawing: a table in a table cell, which the model cannot hold (a
cell holds inlines), and which is a drawing, not data.  It becomes a \code
... \endcode block, the spec's own preformatted display, with the same
labels in the same places, so that the drawing stays readable in any
rendering; the caption below keeps its line.  Lines 575-590 stay 16 lines:
\code, the drawing, \endcode and three comment lines.  The dots of the real
axis are plain periods, the imaginary axis is a column of colons.
--- concept-numbers.tex
+++ concept-numbers.tex
